# GRAPH STRUCTURE
# ---------------
# The graph has three similar blocks. Each is a subdivided K_4,4:
#
#   block 0: L = 0..3,   R = 4..7,   P = 24..39
#   block 1: L = 8..11,  R = 12..15, P = 40..55
#   block 2: L = 16..19, R = 20..23, P = 56..71
#
# Vertices 72..103 are connectors, called M vertices.
#
# Within a block, every P vertex lies between one L branch and one R branch.
# It also has two M neighbors. Every M vertex connects to one P in each block
# and to one other M vertex in the final matching section. This makes every
# vertex degree 4.
#
# The edge list is grouped as follows:
#   1. Internal L-P and R-P edges for blocks 0, 1, and 2 (96 edges)
#   2. Connector-to-P edges for blocks 0, 1, and 2 (96 edges)
#   3. Connector matching edges (16 edges)
# ============================================================================
